{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 3873464,
  "courseSlug": "nextjs-react-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Next.js & React - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "43340694",
      "title": "Building APIs with Route Handlers",
      "lectureOrder": 154,
      "videoOrder": 142,
      "sourceHash": "f35f76075f1c62835ec47e8b950bd2b8b40d3025336b81835411ecb4a2ace900",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.66,
          "end": 3.12,
          "en": "Now with route groups out of the way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.12,
          "end": 7.47,
          "en": "there are just two more important route related features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.47,
          "end": 9.48,
          "en": "I want to introduce you to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.48,
          "end": 13.32,
          "en": "And the first feature, which we won't need in this app here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.32,
          "end": 15.21,
          "en": "but which you still should know,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.21,
          "end": 18.15,
          "en": "are so-called Route Handlers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.15,
          "end": 20.46,
          "en": "For that, I'll set up another path,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.46,
          "end": 23.7,
          "en": "another route path, and I'll do it next to my route groups",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.7,
          "end": 25.86,
          "en": "because it actually won't belong to any",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.86,
          "end": 27.12,
          "en": "of these route groups",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 27.12,
          "end": 30.48,
          "en": "because it won't render an ordinary page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.48,
          "end": 33.93,
          "en": "and therefore it won't need a layout.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 33.93,
          "end": 36.69,
          "en": "And I'll name that path API though the name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 36.69,
          "end": 38.79,
          "en": "as always is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 38.79,
          "end": 42.39,
          "en": "But in there I'll now not add a page.js file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 42.39,
          "end": 43.62,
          "en": "That wouldn't work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 43.62,
          "end": 45.96,
          "en": "because we wouldn't have a layout for that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 45.96,
          "end": 48.42,
          "en": "if it's outside of one of these route groups.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 48.42,
          "end": 51.45,
          "en": "Instead, I'll name it route.js,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 51.45,
          "end": 55.92,
          "en": "which is another reserved name NextJS is looking for.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 55.92,
          "end": 58.14,
          "en": "But with a route.js file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 58.14,
          "end": 60.87,
          "en": "you set up a so-called Route Handler,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 60.87,
          "end": 63.15,
          "en": "which is different from a page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 63.15,
          "end": 65.013,
          "en": "Now, what is a Route Handler though?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 66.09,
          "end": 68.03999999999999,
          "en": "A Route Handler is a file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 68.03999999999999,
          "end": 71.78999999999999,
          "en": "in which you can export various functions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 71.78999999999999,
          "end": 76.78999999999999,
          "en": "which must be named GET or POST or PATCH or PUT",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 79.65,
          "end": 81.53999999999999,
          "en": "or DELETE and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 81.53999999999999,
          "end": 83.03999999999999,
          "en": "So as you can tell,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 83.03999999999999,
          "end": 86.65,
          "en": "which must have an HtDP method name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 87.69,
          "end": 90.24,
          "en": "because the idea behind Route Handlers is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 90.24,
          "end": 93.9,
          "en": "that you can set up routes that don't return pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 93.9,
          "end": 95.75999999999999,
          "en": "that are rendered on the screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 95.75999999999999,
          "end": 98.34,
          "en": "but instead in there in such Route Handlers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 98.34,
          "end": 102.03,
          "en": "you would typically return JSON data, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 102.03,
          "end": 104.55,
          "en": "or you would accept incoming JSON data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 104.55,
          "end": 106.83,
          "en": "and return some JSON response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 106.83,
          "end": 110.16,
          "en": "So the idea behind these Route Handlers is simply",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 110.16,
          "end": 114.63,
          "en": "that you can set up API like routes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 114.63,
          "end": 119.19,
          "en": "which produce data, store data, do whatever you need to do,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 119.19,
          "end": 120.96,
          "en": "but which essentially are called",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 120.96,
          "end": 123.72,
          "en": "behind the scenes from some client.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 123.72,
          "end": 127.86,
          "en": "So from a mobile app or maybe even from one of your pages,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 127.86,
          "end": 130.68,
          "en": "but not to render the overall page content,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 130.68,
          "end": 134.61,
          "en": "but maybe just to store some data behind the scenes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 134.61,
          "end": 137.4,
          "en": "And you can set up multiple Route Handlers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 137.4,
          "end": 141.21,
          "en": "in the same file here to handle different kinds of requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 141.21,
          "end": 143.073,
          "en": "for one in the same path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 144.48,
          "end": 146.1,
          "en": "Now these Route Handlers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 146.1,
          "end": 149.97,
          "en": "will automatically receive a request object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 149.97,
          "end": 152.8,
          "en": "so that will be passed in by NextJS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 154.62,
          "end": 157.17000000000002,
          "en": "and I'll simply log it here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 157.17000000000002,
          "end": 159.18,
          "en": "so that we can see what's inside.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 159.18,
          "end": 161.37,
          "en": "Of course, you also find all the details",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 161.37,
          "end": 162.94,
          "en": "in the official documentation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 164.04,
          "end": 166.92000000000002,
          "en": "and they should then return a response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 166.92000000000002,
          "end": 170.43,
          "en": "And for that you can construct a new response object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 170.43,
          "end": 172.53,
          "en": "using the default response class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 172.53,
          "end": 175.68,
          "en": "that's provided out of the box by the browser",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 175.68,
          "end": 177.513,
          "en": "and by node.js.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 178.44,
          "end": 181.95,
          "en": "And here you could either return some JSON response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 181.95,
          "end": 186.95,
          "en": "or also just some plain text, which is what I'll do here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 186.99,
          "end": 189.93,
          "en": "JSON response could be returned with help",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 189.93,
          "end": 192.3,
          "en": "of the JSON utility method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 192.3,
          "end": 195.42,
          "en": "that can be called directly on the response class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 195.42,
          "end": 196.98,
          "en": "by the way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 196.98,
          "end": 198.66,
          "en": "But here, I'll just return this text",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 198.66,
          "end": 201.57,
          "en": "and I'll comment out this POST Route Handler",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 201.57,
          "end": 205.5,
          "en": "since here I don't wanna handle POST requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 205.5,
          "end": 208.71,
          "en": "But with such a Route Handler added in this case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 208.71,
          "end": 212.43,
          "en": "for a GET request, we can of course still send a request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 212.43,
          "end": 215.31,
          "en": "to it and we can simply send a GET request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 215.31,
          "end": 217.86,
          "en": "by entering the path in our browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 217.86,
          "end": 220.53,
          "en": "So in this case to /api,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 220.53,
          "end": 224.57999999999998,
          "en": "because that's the path name I chose here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 224.57999999999998,
          "end": 229.05,
          "en": "And you will see that you see this Hello! text here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 229.05,
          "end": 233.16,
          "en": "which is indeed the text I am returning as a response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 233.16,
          "end": 236.88,
          "en": "And if you open that server site terminal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 236.88,
          "end": 239.79,
          "en": "you will see a lot of output there, which is essentially",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 239.79,
          "end": 243.81,
          "en": "that request object which is being output.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 243.81,
          "end": 245.52,
          "en": "And you'll see that from that object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 245.52,
          "end": 248.4,
          "en": "you could get information like the method used,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 248.4,
          "end": 251.91,
          "en": "which is not too surprising since we filter requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 251.91,
          "end": 255.45,
          "en": "by picking an appropriate name for our function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 255.45,
          "end": 258.12,
          "en": "But we could also extract a request body",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 258.12,
          "end": 259.47,
          "en": "if there would be any,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 259.47,
          "end": 262.71,
          "en": "so that we could store data in a database, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 262.71,
          "end": 265.89,
          "en": "and extract any other information we might need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 265.89,
          "end": 268.53,
          "en": "from that incoming request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 268.53,
          "end": 270.96,
          "en": "And therefore, even though we don't need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 270.96,
          "end": 273.09000000000003,
          "en": "that Route Handler feature here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 273.09000000000003,
          "end": 276.72,
          "en": "and you might in general not need it too often",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 276.72,
          "end": 280.23,
          "en": "when building a NextJS application, it's important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 280.23,
          "end": 282.03,
          "en": "to know about this feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 282.03,
          "end": 286.08,
          "en": "because it can be really helpful, especially if you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 286.08,
          "end": 289.44,
          "en": "for example, also want to connect our clients",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 289.44,
          "end": 291.84000000000003,
          "en": "to your NextJS application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 291.84000000000003,
          "end": 294.24,
          "en": "So if you're building a NextJS application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 294.24,
          "end": 297.45,
          "en": "that should not just render its pages and so on,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 297.45,
          "end": 300.18,
          "en": "but that should maybe also deliver data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 300.18,
          "end": 303.75,
          "en": "to some mobile app which sends requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 303.75,
          "end": 306.69,
          "en": "to this NextJS application, well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 306.69,
          "end": 308.91,
          "en": "you could then build such Route Handlers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 308.91,
          "end": 310.65,
          "en": "which handle the communication",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 310.65,
          "end": 313.803,
          "en": "with such an external client, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
